   "stem": {
      "text": "Find the exact value of \\( \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{4}{(2n-1)(2n+1)} \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 2
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Partial fractions give \\( \\frac{4}{(2n-1)(2n+1)} = \\frac{2}{2n-1} - \\frac{2}{2n+1} \\), so the series telescopes.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Divide",
               2,
               [
                  "Add",
                  [
                     "Multiply",
                     2,
                     "n"
                  ],
                  -1
               ]
            ],
            [
               "Negate",
               [
                  "Divide",
                  2,
                  [
                     "Add",
                     [
                        "Multiply",
                        2,
                        "n"
                     ],
                     1
                  ]
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Writing out the terms from \\( n = 1 \\) to \\( n = N \\), the inner terms cancel and the partial sum is \\( S_N = 2 - \\frac{2}{2 N + 1} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            2,
            [
               "Negate",
               [
                  "Divide",
                  2,
                  [
                     "Add",
                     [
                        "Multiply",
                        2,
                        "N"
                     ],
                     1
                  ]
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "As \\( N \\to \\infty \\), the terms containing \\( N \\) approach their limits, so \\( \\lim_{N \\to \\infty} S_N = 2 \\).",
         "mathjson": 2
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The value of the series is \\( 2 \\).",
         "mathjson": 2
      }
   ],
